Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 10:54:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 058/154] feat: build a window's sidebar the first time it
 presents, not at birth
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A hidden-pool profile (show=false) built and navigated its sidebar WebContents
in the constructor whether or not it would ever be shown - real renderer work
for a surface nobody was looking at, paid at boot, competing with every other
profile's construction. Its tab/title/favicon churn then rebuilt that model on
every event, still off screen.

PushSidebarSnapshot now asks SlotPresentationTable who is presenting and skips
the rebuild when this window is not. The construction-time BuildHtmlSidebar
call is gone; CatchUpSidebarForNewPresenter is the one funnel every "this
window just became its slot's presenter" site calls instead - the self-creating
ctor's show block, ActivateWindow's first-activation branch, and
NotifyShownIfAdopted. It builds (idempotently) and pushes once, coalescing
whatever the window missed while it was hidden.

ActivateWindow's in-window swap needed an explicit push too: the presenter does
not change there, so the is_presenter gate never re-fires, but `visible_` moved
and the on-screen sidebar was left showing the outgoing tab strip.

The gate itself is a free function in its own target so it is a fast unit test
with no views:: or content:: dependency - a bool in, an enum out.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn b/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn
index e1d238b23256b..7c058ea15d0d8 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn
@@ -630,6 +630,7 @@ static_library("ui") {
     "//chrome/browser/ui/atrium:tab_cycle",
     "//chrome/browser/ui/atrium:peek_decision",
     "//chrome/browser/ui/atrium:restore_plan",
+    "//chrome/browser/ui/atrium:sidebar_snapshot_gate",
     "//chrome/browser/ui/atrium:slot_presentation_table",
     "//chrome/browser/ui/atrium:status_bubble_color_math",
     "//chrome/browser/ui/atrium:surface_key_route",
